# Definition of Done — <feature / change name>

`spec.md` §12 already contains the per-work-item Definition of Done. This template is for cases
where you want a **standalone** DoD outside the SoMi `.somi/plans/<slug>/` artifact set (e.g., a
team-level "shipping standard" checklist). For most work items, fill out §12 of `spec.md`
directly and ignore this file.

## Minimum-evidence standard

A box may be ticked only against evidence of a **stated kind** and a **stated quantity**. Write both
next to the criterion before you start, not after the result is in.

- **Kind** — a named test, a command and its expected output, or a described manual exercise.
  "Verify before ticking" is not a standard: it names no evidence, so any result satisfies it.
- **Quantity** — one run or N runs; one file or every file in a set; one host or each supported
  host. State N, and say why N is enough to tell "works" from "fails some of the time".
- Evidence of the wrong kind, or too small a quantity, does **not** satisfy the criterion even when
  it is green. A passing result that could not have failed proves nothing.

Worked example — a latency claim:

- Weak: `[ ] Checkout p95 latency is under 300 ms (verified).`
  Ticked after two runs, both under 300 ms. If the real failure rate is around 40%, two runs
  pass together about a third of the time, so the green result says almost nothing.
- Fixed: `[ ] Checkout p95 latency is under 300 ms. Evidence: load-test command <cmd>, 20 runs on
  the staging host, p95 reported per run; all 20 under 300 ms. Fewer than 20 runs, or a run on a
  developer machine, does not count.`

If the evidence you can produce is smaller than the criterion needs, leave the box unticked and
say what is missing.

## Functional

- [ ] All planned iterations landed (per `phases/`).
- [ ] Acceptance criteria from each iteration met.
- [ ] Manual verification of golden path completed.
- [ ] Edge cases identified during planning are exercised.

## Tests

- [ ] Unit tests added/updated for changed logic.
- [ ] Integration tests cover the new seam(s).
- [ ] E2E updated if a user-visible journey changed.
- [ ] CI is green on the branch.
- [ ] No skipped/quarantined tests added in this change.

## Code review

- [ ] `/review` run; no unresolved Blockers or Majors in `.somi/reviews/<slug>/`.
- [ ] `security-reviewer` consulted if `spec.md` §8 flagged it.
- [ ] `architecture-reviewer` consulted if a new contract / module / service was introduced.

## Security

- [ ] OWASP categories from `spec.md` §8 addressed in code (not deferred).
- [ ] Secrets handled via the project's secret manager (not committed, not logged).
- [ ] AuthN/AuthZ checks present at every new ingress.
- [ ] Input validation at trust boundaries.
- [ ] No new sinks reachable from untrusted input without explicit mitigation.

## Observability

- [ ] Logs from `spec.md` §9 emit on the relevant paths.
- [ ] Metrics from `spec.md` §9 registered; no high-cardinality labels.
- [ ] Traces propagated across any new RPC/queue hops.
- [ ] Alerts (if any) have runbooks linked.

## Rollout

- [ ] Feature flag (if any) defaults to safe value.
- [ ] Deploy plan from `spec.md` §10 followed.
- [ ] Success metric green for <stated window>.
- [ ] Rollback path verified (at least dry-runnable).

## Documentation

- [ ] User-facing docs updated where behavior changed.
- [ ] Internal architecture docs updated where structure changed.
- [ ] ADR written if a structural decision was made.

## Hygiene

- [ ] No leftover `TODO(claude)` / `FIXME(claude)` without a follow-up issue.
- [ ] No commented-out code, debug prints, or scratch files in the diff.
- [ ] Follow-ups filed (linked below).

